msgstr ""

#. module: l10n_ca_ns_payroll
#: model:l10n_ca.payroll.source,summary:l10n_ca_ns_payroll.source_wcb_ns_maximum
msgid ""
"Maximum assessable earnings per worker, effective January 1: 76,300 in 2025,"
" 79,900 in 2026, 83,300 in 2027; 135.7% of the Nova Scotia average "
"industrial wage. Employers pay premiums only on the earnings of a worker up "
"to the maximum."
msgstr ""

#. module: l10n_ca_ns_payroll
#: model:l10n_ca.payroll.source,summary:l10n_ca_ns_payroll.source_workers_compensation_act
msgid ""
"Maximum gross annual earnings: a percentage of the average industrial wage "
"for the Province set by the Governor in Council (s. 41(c)); the payroll on "
"which the Board assesses an employer excludes the remuneration of a worker "
"above that maximum (s. 124(2))."
msgstr ""

#. module: l10n_ca_ns_payroll
#: model:l10n_ca.payroll.source,summary:l10n_ca_ns_payroll.source_wcb_ns_payment
msgid ""
"Monthly or quarterly report of the assessable payroll, by pay date, with the"
" payment, due the 15th of the month that follows the reporting period, even "
"for a nil payroll."
msgstr ""

